    "content_note": "NACA faired curves only, no symbols, for wings 1, 2 and 3 (47 deg sweep; 4, 6 and 9 percent thick), each labelled with its wing number at both ends ('Wing 2 1 3' from top to bottom on the left, '3 2 1' from top to bottom on the right). All three curves start at M = 0.50 and end at about M = 1.122. Each curve is solid up to about M = 1.04, dashed from about M = 1.045 to about M = 1.09 (two dashes and gaps), then solid to its end. Subsonic order from the top: wing 2 (just below the C_D0 = 0.01 line), wing 1, wing 3; the three curves converge and cross between M = 0.89 and 0.94, where they run inside one band of ink with the C_D0 = 0.01 line."
